master` (71a9948157dc2d5cc71fcb456c9d96656678757d)\n- Not reproducible in Godot 4.5-dev5 and earlier\n- Not reproducible in Godot 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid - Meta Quest 3 - OpenGL API OpenGL ES 3.2 - Compatibility - Using Device: Qualcomm - Adreno (TM) 740\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you have an OpenXR app that positions its controllers or hand models using the \"Aim\" pose, when run with Godot 4.5-beta1 or later, they will be rotated around in an unexpected, different from earlier versions of Godot.\n\nI tested with the [Museum of All Things](https://github.com/m4ym4y/museum-of-all-things), holding my hands in the same position (palms pointed towards my face).\n\n**Godot 4.5-dev5:**\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11b94ac7-c636-4084-9177-1233f7bdfbc7)\n\n**Godot 4.5-beta1:**\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73dfa3df-a2c5-45a4-aaba-c3bee15c2f6b)\n\nThis appears to be caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107386\n\nIf I use `master` but revert just that PR (and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107388 which depends on it), then the hand orientation is as expected again\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open any OpenXR project with hands/controllers (that are complex enough to see if they are rotated) using the \"Aim\" pose to position them\n2. Launch with Godot 4.5-beta1 or later\n3. Notice that the controllers aren't in the right orientation\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMOAT isn't exactly minimal, but I think the [XR Tools demo](https://github.com/GodotVR/godot-xr-tools) would show it as well","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/ot